    "created_at": "2025-06-16T13:04:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-16T13:04:36Z",
    "body": "Yes.\n\nI think Edge Legacy is dead. [Edge Legacy was EOL'd in 2021](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Edge_Legacy#:~:text=The%20end,by%20New%20Edge%2E%5B4%5D) and [it's not possible to launch it](https://www.tenforums.com/browsers-email/198095-there-any-way-still-run-edge-legacy-windows-10-11-a.html#post2466714) (without disabling Code Integrity Checks).\n\nHowever, Internet Explorer might still have non-zero usage and Edge has an [Internet Explorer mode](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/internet-explorer-mode-in-microsoft-edge-6604162f-e38a-48b2-acd2-682dbac6f0de) which will be [supported until at least 2029](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer?utm_source=chatgpt.com#:~:text=The%20core%20of%20Internet%20Explorer%2011%20will%20continue%20being%20shipped%20and%20supported%20until%20at%20least%202029%20as%20IE%20Mode).\n\nLet's keep it conforming for now and revisit in 2030?",
